===Admire the sword{{subst:void|<!--202200603-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

:{{DIcon|Изучение}} Investigate
:{{tx}}
:'''Huaiyan:''' There will be numerous contests and celebrations during the Wardance, and the main event will be the Ringmaster's Challenge.
:'''Huaiyan:''' The host will dispatch a skilled warrior to take on challengers from all over the cosmos, showcasing the excellent martial arts of the Xianzhou Luofu. When you mentioned that the Astral Express would be attending the ceremony, I thought the high elder of the Luofu would be the ringmaster...
:'''Jing Yuan:''' You humor me, Elder Huaiyan. The Healer Lady is just a young lady who knows nothing about martial arts. How can I assign her as the ringmaster?
:'''Huaiyan:''' I'm no match to you when it comes to joking.
:'''March 7th:''' What's this box for? Why don't you open it, General Huaiyan?
:'''Huaiyan:''' This sword case is intended for the Wardance's award. It's empty now, but in a few days, a precious sword will be delivered and stored inside.
:'''Huaiyan:''' I don't mean to boast about our skills, but this sword represents the pinnacle of the Zhuming's craftsmanship. It has a legendary history, full of heroic tales from foreign lands, tales that are too detailed to be summarized in just a few words. Since the delegation delivering the sword hasn't arrived yet, I'll just leave the case here for now.
:'''Huaiyan:''' I've been wondering... who would be worthy of such a sword? And then it hit me &mdash; I can award it to the champion of the Ringmaster's Challenge! The ceremony's champion is sure to be a perfect match for the sword.
:'''Huaiyan:''' Moreover, I hear that Yanqing is an excellent swordmaster, and that he will be representing the Luofu as the ringmaster, so it seems like a perfect gift for him.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Thank you for your generosity, Elder Huaiyan.
:'''Yunli:''' If you want to give me a sword, just say the word, Grandpa. No need to beat around the bush.
:'''Huaiyan:''' You've got confidence, my girl, but I don't think you can best Yanqing.
:'''Yanqing:''' I know you're all about swords, Miss Yunli. It's just a shame that it's the sword that ultimately chooses its rightful master.
:'''Yunli:''' Yeah, and even if someone gets their hands on such a precious sword, it'll probably end up in someone else's.
:'''Yanqing:''' The outcome of our duel at the Alchemy Commission is still up in the air. Since you're interested, why don't you represent the Xianzhou Zhuming and challenge me in the ring?
:'''Yunli:''' That's exactly what I had in mind! Nobody knows who's gonna come out on top! It could be me, could be someone else... It'll probably be me, but whatever happens... it won't be him!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Looks like Feixiao was right.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It'll be either death or disaster when these two clash...
:'''March 7th:''' Not to be rude or anything... We've been watching their drama. I'm dying to find out who beats who.
:'''Huaiyan:''' Quiet down! We have other guests here! I've prepared this sword to add some excitement to the ceremony, not to have you two squabble. It's not a good look for the Alliance.
:'''Huaiyan:''' While you both seem confident that you'll win, you need to remember there can only be one winner and one loser in the ring, which could lead to hard feelings. Actually, I have an idea...
:'''Huaiyan:''' We don't know who the winner will be, and it might not be either of you, but if you're eyeing that prize, you'll need to work together. I want you to take on an apprentice who will take part in the Wardance and win at least one match.
:'''Yunli & Yanqing:''' How does that make sense?
:'''Huaiyan:''' In my humble opinion, while a Cloud Knight is commendable by securing victories, it's even more so to pass on your skills and spread the way of swordplay.
:'''Huaiyan:''' I'd be greatly pleased if this apprentice could represent the Express in the Wardance by displaying their Cloud Knight flair and prowess.
:'''Jing Yuan:''' Well, Elder Huaiyan's idea is quite interesting. Imparting swordplay skills requires teamwork, and both the winner and the loser will learn a valuable lesson regardless of the outcome. The question is, whom should the two of them take as an apprentice?
:'''March 7th:''' Huh? Who? Wait, me...?
:'''Huaiyan:''' I noticed just now that Miss March seemed quite interested in the outcome of your sword fight, so I thought why not teach her the art of swordplay?
:'''March 7th:''' ...Huh? Wait! Are you serious, General?
:'''March 7th:''' Why am I being dragged into this all of a sudden? I've never practiced swordplay before! I'm a total newbie! You really think I can learn it? You'll probably realize I have no hope and give up on me, and that'd be sooo embarrassing!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why don't you choose Dan Heng?
::'''Dan Heng:''' Things are already complicated enough as they are, (Trailblazer).
::'''Huaiyan:''' He strikes like lightning... Does Mr. Dan Heng really need anyone's guidance?
::'''Huaiyan:''' As for Miss March... she's like a piece of jade in the rough, just waiting to be shaped.
::Why don't you choose me?
::'''Huaiyan:''' Your talent is quite... unique. Are you also interested in swordplay?
::'''Huaiyan:''' But you know, based on my years of judging people, you don't really need to dive into swordplay to boost your skills... and I doubt there's anyone out there who can really show you the way forward.
::'''Huaiyan:''' As for Miss March... she's like a piece of jade in the rough, just waiting to be shaped.
::Just accept your fate, March!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why don't you choose me?
